-- RUM Group Inc. (rum-group)
-- Last verified: 2026-09-23T00:00:00+00:00
-- ============================================================

INSERT INTO research_companies (slug, legal_name, jurisdiction, operational_hq, primary_archetype, self_described_archetype, reporting_standard, functional_currency, presentation_currency, financial_year_end, tier, expected_disclosure_cadence, market_cap_band, funding_source, acn, abn, arbn, isin, lei, curator_notes, last_verified_at, is_published)
SELECT
  'rum-group',
  'RUM Group Inc.',
  'unknown',
  NULL,
  'treasury_allocation',
  'treasury_allocation',
  'us_gaap',
  'USD',
  'USD',
  '12-31',
  'peer_shaped',
  'quarterly',
  NULL,
  'balance_sheet',
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  $q$Asked for as Rumble Inc. The quarterly report for the period ended 30 June 2026 is filed by RUM Group Inc.; the March 2026 quarterly was filed as Rumble Inc. Same SEC registrant throughout, CIK 1830081. Eighth record, eighth identifier change.

The reason this record is worth keeping is what the trackers say about it. Three public bitcoin trackers sighted today report this company at 210.8 or 211 BTC, two of them stamped "as of 8 May 2025" or "latest purchase May 2025". The company's own Q2 2026 reporting, as relayed by trade press, puts the holding at 293.14 BTC after adding 82.32 during the quarter — roughly 39% more coins than every tracker shows. Anyone pricing this company off aggregated data is working from a figure nine months stale and understated by a quarter. This is the failure mode the register was built to prevent, and it is the first time we have caught it live rather than in a dossier's postmortem.

And the gate blocks all of it, again. Everything verifiable here — 210.82 BTC at 31 March 2026 and 31 December 2025, cost basis $19,100,000, fair value $14,384,759 at 31 March 2026 against $18,450,362 three months earlier, the full reconciliation of purchases and fair value movements, the fair value hierarchy treatment — sits in 10-Qs at rank 3 against the rank 2 a ledger event requires. That is two records in a row and the sixth overall. Angel Studios makes the argument more cleanly; this one adds that the refused disclosure is also the only accurate source in existence, because the free trackers are wrong and the company does not issue exchange-style holdings announcements.

One genuinely new wrinkle: the Q2 2026 accounts show digital assets other than bitcoin — eIOU tokens acquired as part of the NDAG acquisition, classified at Level 3 of the fair value hierarchy. Tokens arriving through M&A rather than through a treasury decision, and illiquid enough to be marked with unobservable inputs. The register models bitcoin holdings and has no way to record that a company also holds something it never chose to buy and cannot price from a quoted market. For a CFO the lesson is narrower and sharper: a bitcoin treasury policy does not scope what lands on the balance sheet when you buy a company.

Scale, for context and not for comparison: the position is reported at under 8% of total liquidity, with the rest in conventional instruments. This is a treasury allocation in the plain sense — the thing most Australian mid-market boards are actually contemplating — rather than a treasury company.

Restricted and worth naming: trackers publish mNAV figures for this company between 160x and 180x. The number is arithmetically true and analytically meaningless — it divides a two-billion-dollar market capitalisation by a fourteen-million-dollar bitcoin position for a business whose value has nothing to do with its bitcoin. Never publish it, and treat its appearance on a tracker page as a reason to distrust the rest of that page.

Identity: jurisdiction recorded as "unknown" for the same reason as Hamak — the column is NOT NULL and no sighted document states the state or country of incorporation. Secondary descriptions call the company Canadian and Canadian-American; the filings are US domestic forms. Two conflicting stories, neither confirmed here.

Gaps: the Q2 2026 holding of 293.14 BTC is registered as a document but the figure reaches this record through trade press, so it is not stored; no custody disclosure sighted; the November 2024 policy announcement and the early 2025 purchase of about 188 BTC at roughly $91,000 have no registered primary source.$q$,
  '2026-09-23T00:00:00+00:00',
  FALSE
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM research_companies WHERE slug = 'rum-group');

